<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The app's own theme, and the reason the site knows whether the phone is
     light or dark.

     From targetSdk 33 onwards a WebView does not ask the system about dark
     mode: it reads android:isLightTheme off the theme of the activity it sits
     in, and reports that to the page as prefers-color-scheme. Bubblewrap gives
     every activity the application theme, Theme.Translucent.NoTitleBar, which
     descends from the original dark Theme — so Dvarim rendered dark on a phone
     in light mode, and nothing in the web app could tell it otherwise.

     A day/night pair settles it: this file is the light half, res/values-night
     the dark one, and Android picks. Switching the phone recreates the activity,
     which is what makes the site follow along.

     windowBackground is the web app's own page colour, so a cold start does not
     flash white, and windowLightStatusBar keeps the clock and battery readable
     against it. -->
